HostMot2 Smart Serial software regression tests
=============================================

These compile the production drivers with mock LLIO and HAL storage. No
hardware is accessed. Run after configuring/building a run-in-place tree:

    scripts/rip-environment runtests tests/hostmot2/sserial
    SANITIZERS=address,undefined bash tests/hostmot2/sserial/test.sh

CC can select another C compiler. Sanitizers are optional.

Coverage: format/name bounds, failed realloc preserving existing data,
encoder H format, string termination/case conversion, repeated cleanup,
parameter comparison at 32/64-bit precision (including NaN, infinity and
signed zero), unsupported widths, byte-reader success/error values, and
Smart Serial/Smart Serial B discovery with empty leading ports and disabled
trailing ports (including GPIO pin allocation).

These are not hardware validation. Before approval, record the tested commit,
board and remote model, firmware, HAL configuration, and observed results for:
discovery with an empty first port; normal process I/O; volatile/nonvolatile
parameter writes; reconnect/error recovery; repeated load/unload; and the
applicable SSI/BiSS/Fanuc encoder paths. Firmware flashing remains untested
on hardware. The setup-mode failure-state changes from #4144 are excluded.
